\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33588583676535866, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14942528823622667, \"vector_similarity\": 0.77096045, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**trask** — 2025-12-01T18:36:48Z\\n\\n@jaydeluca updating from `main` should resolve the link failure\\n\\n---\\n\\n**svrnm** — 2025-12-02T08:40:24Z\\n\\n🎉 \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-02]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Project Proposal: Ecosystem Explorer (open-telemetry/community#3000)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000  \\n\\n**Author**: jaydeluca  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-09-19T10:11:57Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-02T08:40:24Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-12-01T19:04:18Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `instrumentation-docs` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +251 / -0 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: area/project-proposal  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Reviews (15)\\n\\n**svrnm** — CHANGES_REQUESTED — 2025-09-19T12:02:17Z\\n\\nThanks for leading this @jaydeluca -- this also replaces https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/2246\\n\\n**mx-psi** — COMMENTED — 2025-09-19T12:29:51Z\\n\\nIs the Collector intentionally out of scope? From the discussions I have had with @svrnm it seems like this should be similar enough (instead of libraries we would be talking about components), so I feel like it would be a good idea to include it as well\\n\\n**mx-psi** — COMMENTED — 2025-10-29T12:17:34Z\\n\\n**vitorvasc** — COMMENTED — 2025-10-30T15:07:24Z\\n\\n**svrnm** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-18T07:55:05Z\\n\\n**svrnm** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-18T07:58:54Z\\n\\n**svrnm** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-18T07:59:07Z\\n\\n**svrnm** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-18T08:00:13Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"trask 2025 12 01t18 36 48z jaydeluca updat from main should resolv the link failur svrnm 2025 12 02t08 40 24z sourc id src pr 02 pull request project propos ecosystem explor open telemetri communiti 3000 canon url http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000 author jaydeluca creat 2025 09 19t10 11 57z updat 2025 12 02t08 40 24z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 01t19 04 18z branch instrument doc main chang 251 0 across 2 file label area project propos mileston review 15 svrnm chang _ request 2025 09 19t12 02 17z thank for lead this jaydeluca this also replac http github com open telemetri communiti pull 2246 mx psi comment 2025 09 19t12 29 51z is the collector intent out of scope from the discuss i have had with svrnm it seem like this should be similar enough instead of librari we would be talk about compon so i feel like it would be a good idea to includ it a well mx psi comment 2025 10 29t12 17 34z vitorvasc comment 2025 10 30t15 07 24z svrnm comment 2025 11 18t07 55 05z svrnm comment 2025 11 18t07 58 54z svrnm comment 2025 11 18t07 59 07z svrnm comment 2025 11 18t08 00 13z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"676128d64083cc7b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33253092176535864, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14942528823622667, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7597774, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"To summarise I feel it is beneficial to be using weaver to document/describe the signals as well as the instrumentation emitting them as they should be sharing significant amounts of data. This way the eco-system Explorer can then focus on presenting and making discoverable the emitted definitions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**jack-berg** — 2025-11-10T15:29:30Z\\n\\nWhen I read this proposal, I see this project as a an attempt to build a new registry (registry 2.0). I'm very supportive of this as I've been complaining about various deficiencies of the registry for some time.\\n\\nSignificantly, the proposal is to launch the new effort in parallel to the existing registry, allowing the contributors to iterate quickly and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gathering.\\n\\nLater, once we've worked out the sharp edges, we can merge registry 1.0 into registry 2.0, and EOL registry 1.0.\\n\\nSome thoughts:\\n\\n- The registry already has a data model for capturing meta data about components (schema [here](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry.io)), but its insufficient. As you note, there's all sorts of data which is important to capture and visualize for end users, which as of now, is very difficult for users to discover. The key examples being: configuration schema, schema of telemetry emitted, instructions on how to get started.\\n\\n- The [registry](https://opentelemetry.io/ecosystem/registry/) already has tools for searching for components, and displaying bits of information about them, but its insufficient. More than anything else, the registry is an index of links, requiring the user to follow the link and find installation / configuration / telemetry schema details in the linked website / repository. Except this information is no always available, and when it is, there's no standardization about the display. A richer registry schema would allow a richer / more useful visualization experience.\\n\\n- The registry already has [tooling](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry.io/blob/main/scripts/registry-scanner/index.mjs) for scanning for project repositories and creating / updating registry component entries. The problem is, its all centralized in the `opentelemetry.io` project and standardized, meaning that its only possible to scrape the types of meta data which can scraped from a central script. In his prototype, @jaydeluca has built tooling which leverages domain knowledge specific to the `opentelemetry-java-instrumentation` project, and is therefore able to generate much richer meta data that is captured by the registry today. Any effort for a better registry is probably going to require some coordination between the repos where components live (i.e SDK, instrumentation, contrib, collector, etc) and the `opentelemetry.io` repo. Some shared tooling can / should be centralized in `opentelemetry.io`, but the repos should also work to do a better job of publishing the types of meta data that can't be generated through simple scanner scripts.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"to summaris i feel it is benefici to be use weaver to document describ the signal a well a the instrument emit them a they should be share signific amount of data this way the eco system explor can then focus on present and make discover the emit definit jack berg 2025 11 10t15 29 30z when i read this propos i see this project a a an attempt to build a new registri registri 20 i m veri support of this a i ve been complain about various defici of the registri for some time signific the propos is to launch the new effort in parallel to the exist registri allow the contributor to iter quick and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gather later onc we ve work out the sharp edg we can merg registri 10 into registri 20 and eol registri 10 some thought the registri alreadi ha a data model for captur meta data about compon schema here http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io but it insuffici a you note there s all sort of data which is import to captur and visual for end user which a of now is veri difficult for user to discov the key exampl be configur schema schema of telemetri emit instruct on how to get start the registri http opentelemetri io ecosystem registri alreadi ha tool for search for compon and display bit of inform about them but it insuffici more than anyth els the registri is an index of link requir the user to follow the link and find instal configur telemetri schema detail in the link websit repositori except this inform is no alway avail and when it is there s no standard about the display a richer registri schema would allow a richer more use visual experi the registri alreadi ha tool http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io blob main script registri scanner index mjs for scan for project repositori and creat updat registri compon entri the problem is it all central in the opentelemetri io project and standard mean that it onli possibl to scrape the type of meta data which can scrape from a central script in his prototyp jaydeluca ha built tool which leverag domain knowledg specif to the opentelemetri java instrument project and is therefor abl to generat much richer meta data that is captur by the registri today ani effort for a better registri is probabl go to requir some coordin between the repo where compon live i e sdk instrument contrib collector etc and the opentelemetri io repo some share tool can should be central in opentelemetri io but the repo should also work to do a better job of publish the type of meta data that can t be generat through simpl scanner script\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"6aef2203f67ca0d8\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30110632975584617, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11494252965120887, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73548853, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"SyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsEnabled/Float64Histogram/Attributes/0-24               431.0n ± 2%   116.3n ±  2%  -73.01% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsEnabled/Float64Histogram/Attributes/10-24              470.9n ± 1%   171.0n ±  5%  -63.70% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\n```\\n\\nI explored using a []atomic.Pointer[measurement], but this had similar performance while being much more complex (needing a sync.Pool to eliminate allocations).  The single-threaded performance was also much worse for that solution.  See https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/compare/main...dashpole:optimize_histogram_reservoir_old.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-05]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Optimize histogram reservoir (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7443)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/op