 02t13 56 40z updat 2025 12 15t15 00 11z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 15t14 59 34z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8757264a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"id\": \"bd4cf3022c233cd4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.297803075759017, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12643678251288146, \"vector_similarity\": 0.69765776, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8757264a8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7443.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 20034, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:06\", \"token_count\": 7244, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-04]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Use sync.Map and atomics to improve sum performance (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7427)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7427  \\n\\n**Author**: dashpole  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-09-29T14:36:56Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-14T14:40:27Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-10-07T13:40:23Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `optimize_counter_syncmap` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +437 / -121 across 14 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: area:metrics  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.39.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAlternative to https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7380\\n\\nThis uses a sync.Map and atomics for the sum's counter value.  This intentionally introduces a new race condition that didn't previously exist:\\n\\n* It is possible for the exemplar to be recorded in the batch of metrics after the add() for cumulative sum aggregations. For cumulative, this isn't a huge issue since exemplars are expected to persist across collection cycles. This is difficult to fix because we can't manage the internal storage of an exemplar.Reservoir (to atomically swap between hot and cold storage).  If we are able to make assumptions about how exemplar reservoirs are managed (i.e. that the number of and order of exemplars returned is always the same), then we could possibly fix this by merging at export time.\\n\\n### Alternatives Considered\\n\\n#### RWLock for the map instead of sync.Map\\n\\nThis is significantly less performant.\\n\\n#### Single sync.Map without hotColdWaitGroup\\n\\nDeleting keys from the sync.Map concurrently with measurements (during Clear() of the sync.Map) can cause measurements to be made to a counter that has already been read, exported and deleted.  This can produce incorrect sums when delta is used.  Instead, atomically switching writes to a completely empty sync.Map and waiting for writes to the previous sync.Map complete eliminates this issue.\\n\\n#### Use two sync.Map for cumulative sums\\n\\nOne idea I explored was doing a hot-cold swap for cumulative sums just like we do for delta sums.  We would swap the hot and cold sync.Maps, wait for writes to the cold sync.Map to complete while new writes go to the hot map.  Then, once we are done reading the cold map, we could merge the contents of the cold map back into the new hot map.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 04 pull request use sync map and atom to improv sum perform open telemetri opentelemetri go 7427 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7427 author dashpol creat 2025 09 29t14 36 56z updat 2025 10 14t14 40 27z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 10 07t13 40 23z branch optim _ counter _ syncmap main chang 437 121 across 14 file label area metric mileston v1 39 0 descript altern to http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7380 this us a sync map and atom for the sum s counter valu this intent introduc a new race condit that didn t previous exist it is possibl for the exemplar to be record in the batch of metric after the add for cumul sum aggreg for cumul this isn t a huge issu sinc exemplar are expect to persist across collect cycl this is difficult to fix becaus we can t manag the intern storag of an exemplar reservoir to atom swap between hot and cold storag if we are abl to make assumpt about how exemplar reservoir are manag i e that the number of and order of exemplar return is alway the same then we could possibl fix this by merg at export time altern consid rwlock for the map instead of sync map this is signific less perform singl sync map without hotcoldwaitgroup delet key from the sync map concurr with measur dure clear of the sync map can caus measur to be made to a counter that ha alreadi been read export and delet this can produc incorrect sum when delta is use instead atom switch write to a complet empti sync map and wait for write to the previous sync map complet elimin this issu use two sync map for cumul sum one idea i explor wa do a hot cold swap for cumul sum just like we do for delta sum we would swap the hot and cold sync map wait for write to the cold sync map to complet while new write go to the hot map then onc we are done read the cold map we could merg the content of the cold map back into the new hot map\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875c049e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"id\": \"48f382952d1f96ae\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29563117775901704, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12643678251288146, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6904181, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875c049e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 37741, \"chunk_count\": 26, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:02\", \"token_count\": 14705, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**flc1125** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-11T13:20:30Z\\n\\n**flc1125** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-11T13:59:33Z\\n\\n**akats7** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-11T15:42:57Z\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-12T01:28:14Z\\n\\n**akats7** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-12T10:24:52Z\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609  \\n\\n**Author**: Yiling-J  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-01-13T13:45:43Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-13T01:26:12Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/gin_multipartform` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +95 / -0 across 3 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Review Comments (28)\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-13T14:56:36Z\\n\\nI believe the content of `ff` can be detected here.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-13T14:59:10Z\\n\\nassert.NoError?\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 117) — 2025-01-13T15:02:32Z\\n\\nI'm wondering, if there's another middleware layer outside this one, would it be removed because of this?\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-13T15:27:41Z\\n\\nThe goal of the test is to ensure that temporary files are automatically removed, not to test multipart file parsing. The sole purpose of using `c.FormFile` is to trigger multipart parsing, which creates temporary files. I added a `fileHeader.Open()` test in this function to confirm that the temporary file is available. However, I think checking the value of `ff` is unnecessary.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"flc1125 comment 2025 11 11t13 20 30z flc1125 comment 2025 11 11t13 59 33z akats7 comment 2025 11 11t15 42 57z yile j comment 2025 11 12t01 28 14z akats7 comment 2025 11 12t10 24 52z sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 author yile j creat 2025 01 13t13 45 43z updat 2025 11 13t01 26 12z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open branch fix gin _ multipartform main chang 95 0 across 3 file label mileston review comment 28 flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 13t14 56 36z i believ the content of ff can be detect here flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 13t14 59 10z assert noerror flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 117 2025 01 13t15 02 32z i m wonder if there s anoth middlewar layer outsid this one would it be remov becaus of this yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 13t15 27 41z the goal of the test is to ensur that temporari file are automat remov not to test multipart file pars the sole purpos of use c formfil is to trigger multipart pars which creat temporari file i ad a filehead open test in this function to confirm that the temporari file is avail howev i think check the valu of ff is unnecessari\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"05841978e5499c27\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29489656775901696, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12643678251288146, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6879694, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-05]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Optimize histogram reservoir (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7443)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7443  \\n\\n**Author**: dashpole  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-02T13:56:40Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-15T15:00:11Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-12-15T14:59:34Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `optimize_histogram_reservoir` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +173 / -61 across 8 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThis improves the concurrent performance of the histogram reservoir's Offer function by 4x (i.e. 75% reduction).\\n\\nAccomplish this by locking each measurement, rather than locking around the entire storage.  Also, defer extracting the trace context from context.Context until collection time. This improves the performance of Offer, which is on the measure hot path.  Exemplars are often overwritten, so deferring the operation until Collect reduces the overall work.\\n\\n```\\n\\n                           │   main.txt   │              hist.txt              │\\n\\n                           │    sec/op    │   sec/op     vs base               │\\n\\nFixedSizeReservoirOffer-24    211.4n ± 3%   177.5n ± 3%  -16.04% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\nHistogramReservoirOffer-24   200.85n ± 2%   47.41n ± 2%  -76.40% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\ngeomean                       206.1n        91.73n       -55.48%\\n\\n```\\n\\nBenchmarks for Measure:\\n\\n```\\n\\n                                                                                 │  main.txt   │             histres.txt             │\\n\\n                                                                                 │   sec/op    │    sec/op     vs base               │\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsEnabled/Int64Histogram/Attributes/0-24                 436.7n ± 4%   114.8n ±  5%  -73.72% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsEnabled/Int64Histogram/Attributes/10-24                472.2n ± 2%   169.7n ±  8%  -64.08% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 05 pull request optim histogram reservoir open telemetri opentelemetri go 7443 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7443 author dashpol creat 2025 10 02t13 56 40z updat 2025 12 15t15 00 11z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 15t14 59 34z branch optim _ histogram _ reservoir main chang 173 61 across 8 file label mileston v1 400 descript this improv the concurr perform of the histogram reservoir s offer function by 4x i e 75 reduct accomplish this by lock each measur rather than lock around the entir storag also defer extract the trace context from context context until collect time this improv the perform of offer which is on the measur hot path exemplar are often overwritten so defer the oper until collect reduc the overal work main txt hist 